  "question": {
    "text": "If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8712;&#160;</mo><mi>R</mi><mo>&#160;</mo></math> and the equation <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><mn>2</mn><mo>(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>-</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo><mo>)</mo><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>a</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math> (where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>[</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>]</mo></math> denotes the greatest integer <math> <mrow> <mo>&#8804;</mo> </mrow> </math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>x</mi></math>) has no integral solution, then all possible values of&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>&nbsp;lie in the interval&nbsp;",
    "image": null
  },
